      "message": "perf(sim): share unchanged cut bricks between playback keyframes\n\nA playback keyframe was a whole copy of the cut layers. The cut layers\nnow hold each brick in an Arc: a clone copies the keys and the pointers,\nand a write copies a brick first when a clone still holds it. The\nkeyframe store counts a keyframe by the bricks that the keyframe before\nit does not share, and by its map entries. claim_record and up_record\nread the cell first, so a move that changes no cell copies no brick.\n\nDense 100 mm face (release): 68 keyframes hold 65.2 MB; whole copies\ncost 444.9 MB (factor 6.8). The replay stays the live cut bit for bit.\n\nFixes #2194\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
